    "description": "Brightspeed owns and operates wireline telecommunications and fiber broadband infrastructure in the United States. Its customers include residential broadband subscribers, businesses, and wholesale communications counterparties, and the business is investing capital into a largely asset-heavy fiber upgrade program across a legacy local-exchange footprint. Public disclosures describe operations across 20 states and a long-term plan to expand fiber coverage materially within that footprint. The company was formed in connection with Apollo-managed funds' acquisition of Lumen's incumbent local exchange carrier business and launched the Brightspeed brand in 2021 ahead of the transaction close. Mubadala announced a $500 million minority investment in Brightspeed in May 2023. The reviewed public materials do not disclose Mubadala's ownership percentage or the detailed current ownership split among Apollo-managed vehicles.",
